{"name":"Rosetta","hex":"#ba8f7f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Rosetta","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the class Acantharea – certain chromists."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in northern Egypt.","A suburb of Hobart, in the City of Glenorchy, Tasmania, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Rosetta"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosetta","blocks":[{"text":"Rosetta or Rashid is a port city of the Nile Delta, 65 km (40 mi) east of Alexandria, in Egypt's Beheira governorate. The Rosetta Stone was discovered in nearby Fort Julien in 1799."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/RashidNorth.jpg/330px-RashidNorth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosetta","wikidata":"Q243699"},{"title":"Rosetta (spacecraft)","blocks":[{"text":"Rosetta was a space probe built by the European Space Agency that launched on 2 March 2004. Along with Philae, its lander module, Rosetta performed a detailed study of comet 67P/Churyumov–Gerasimenko (67P). During its journey to the comet, the spacecraft performed flybys of Earth, Mars, and the asteroids 21 Lutetia and 2867 Šteins. It was launched as the third cornerstone mission of the ESA's Horizon 2000 programme, after SOHO / Cluster and XMM-Newton. The total cost of the mission was about €1.3 billion (US$1.8 billion)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/95/Rosetta_insignia.png/330px-Rosetta_insignia.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosetta_(spacecraft)","wikidata":"Q48572"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/RashidAbbasiMosque.jpg/500px-RashidAbbasiMosque.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d